<title>USA: GE Engine gains control of Brazilian company.</title>
<headline>GE Engine gains control of Brazilian company.</headline>
<dateline>EVANDALE, Ohio 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>GE Engine Services Inc said Tuesday it has acquired majority control of Celma, a Brazilian company that overhauls and repairs jet engines.</p>
<p>GE, which previously owned 9.7 percent of Celma, will now own about 74 percent of the company. Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Celma is based in Petropolis, Brazil. It is projected to reach sales of more than $140 million in 1996.</p>
<p>GE Engine Services is a wholly owned subsidiary of General Electric Co.</p>
